com_log: cap the daemon log file size instead of growing it forever

com_log_init() opens DAEMON_LOG_PATH/<timestamp>.log with fopen(..., "w")
and log_write() fwrite+fflush's every buffered log line to it for the
whole life of the process -- there is no rotation and no size cap
anywhere in this SDK. ar8030d runs with no CLI flag to reduce log
verbosity (`getopt_long(argc, argv, "p:hU:i:B:P:S:D:", ...)` in
daemon/main.c has no log-level option), and every module defaults to at
least COM_LOG_INFO, so this file grows continuously from ordinary
per-RPC/per-socket-event tracing (nod_read_thread, dev_send_thread,
cb-dat, ...).

On a real Hi3516CV610 air unit this filled a 28.5MB tmpfs-backed /tmp in
well under an hour under ar8030-transport's traffic pattern (much higher
RPC call volume than the plain IP/RNDIS path this SDK was originally
tuned against: per-chunk bb_socket_write, per-poll BB_GET_MCS). Once
/tmp hit 100% the extra tmpfs page usage showed up as system-wide memory
pressure with no single process's RSS looking abnormal, and the kernel
OOM-killer picked essentially arbitrary victims -- in the observed case,
waybeam, which has nothing to do with the actual growth and previously
ran for hours unattended over the IP link before ar8030-transport
existed.

This patch truncates the log file back to empty once it crosses
DAEMON_LOG_MAX_BYTES (2MB) rather than adding rotation/multiple files,
since the log's only real use here is a recent-activity debug trace, not
a persisted history, and a single bounded file is the smallest change
that fixes the unbounded growth.

diff --git a/com/com_log.h b/com/com_log.h
--- a/com/com_log.h
+++ b/com/com_log.h
@@ -6,6 +6,12 @@
 extern "C" {
 #endif
 #define DAEMON_LOG_PATH "daemon_log"
+/* log_write() truncates the log file back to empty once it crosses this
+ * size, since com_log_init() never rotates it: left alone it grows for
+ * the whole life of the daemon and can fill a small tmpfs-backed /tmp
+ * (28.5MB on a Hi3516CV610 air unit), which starves unrelated processes
+ * of memory and gets them OOM-killed instead of ar8030d itself. */
+#define DAEMON_LOG_MAX_BYTES (2 * 1024 * 1024)
 typedef enum {
     COM_LOG_DEBUG = 0,
     COM_LOG_INFO,
diff --git a/com/com_log.c b/com/com_log.c
--- a/com/com_log.c
+++ b/com/com_log.c
@@ -121,6 +121,12 @@ static int log_write(void* pri, void* buff, int len)
     if (log_fp) {
         fwrite(buff, sizeof(char), len, log_fp);
         fflush(log_fp);
+#if !defined(_WIN32)
+        if (ftell(log_fp) > DAEMON_LOG_MAX_BYTES) {
+            rewind(log_fp);
+            ftruncate(fileno(log_fp), 0);
+        }
+#endif
     }
     return len;
 }
